(TIM-22 - `Create a timer called '<name>'.` brings a timer into being
 under a quoted multi-word name, and that name takes the doubled-quote
 possessive `'job timer''s` the manual's examples use throughout.
 Note the `type` line has no `the` in front of it: `the <name>'s type`
 is rejected for every type of variable, not just timers, so it is not a
 claim of this section - see the Report.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox TIM-22.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   Create made a timer
   the created timer ran
)
Create a timer called 'job timer'.
Start the 'job timer'.
Stop the 'job timer'.
If 'job timer''s type is "Timer (static)" then, print "Create made a timer".
Otherwise, print "Create made a {'job timer''s type}".
If the 'job timer''s start time is greater than 0 then, print "the created timer ran".
Otherwise, print "the created timer never started".
